<description>
Fill holes in a target object with colors from a source object's subsprites, then tight-crop.

Input structure:
- bg = background. Two similar 8-connected objects share an outline color.
- Source has colored subsprites in cavities; target has empty cavities.

Rule:
- Find the two 8-connected objects.
- Target = object with more hole area. Align subsprites to holes (rotation/flip if needed).
- Fill each hole with its matched subsprite color; tight-crop.

Key insight: Hole centers in the target are matched to source subsprite centers under the best rotation/flip transform.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "sprite s with colored inner subsprites",
  "dst": "merge with sprite d with holes",
  "match_cond": "s.subsprites.arrangement == d.holes.arrangement",
  "transform": "fill each hole in d with color of corresponding subsprite in s",
  "grid_shape": "tight crop"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task_type: move_to_match
  grid: 22-30 rows x 22-30 cols
  background: single color (any), most frequent in grid
  colors: 1 outline color + 3-7 distinct fill colors, all non-bg
  src:
    desc: single 8-connected object = outline skeleton + colored subsprites filling cavities
    shape: 7-17 rows x 7-13 cols
    outline: LR-symmetric skeleton enclosing all cavities
    cavities:
      count: 4-9 enclosed regions (counted under 4-connectivity on the fill mask)
      shape: arbitrary; ~50% are non-rectangular, including L-shaped, T-shaped,
        staircase, cross-shaped, rectangles with notches, multi-row organic blobs
      bbox: 1-6 rows x 1-11 cols; area 1-38 pixels; can span multiple rows freely
      fill_ratio: 0.5-1.0 of bbox (non-rect cavities fill 50-83% of bbox) [observed]
      packing: cavities pack tightly — neighboring cavities often touch diagonally
        (4-disconnected but 8-connected). This is a core eval pattern: under 8-connectivity
        the fill mask often merges into fewer components than under 4-connectivity.
        Example 1 has 4 4-conn cavities that all merge to 1 under 8-conn.
    subsprites: each cavity fully filled with one fill color (1 subsprite per cavity)
    fill_assignment: mirror-pair cavities share the same fill color by default;
      occasional mismatches allowed (10% of cavities)gai
    connectivity: always 1 connected component (8-connected, outline + fills together)
  dst:
    desc: single 8-connected outline-only object with empty (bg) holes matching src's cavity arrangement
    shape: similar to src (within +/-2 rows/cols)
    outline: same color as src, LR-symmetric skeleton; single 8-connected component
      (may appear as multiple 4-connected pieces due to diagonal pixel adjacencies)
    holes: same count as src subsprites (under 4-connectivity); same relative row/col
      rank ordering of centroids
    hole_shapes: arbitrary shapes with similar diversity as src cavities (mix of rect and
      non-rect). Holes also pack tightly (8-connected merging).
    shape_difference: src subsprite shapes and dst hole shapes MUST be different
    hole_bbox: 1-5 rows x 1-9 cols; area 1-34 pixels [observed]
  placement: src and dst positioned independently on the canvas; their bboxes may spatially
    overlap as long as their pixels don't collide (eval examples show such overlaps)
  transform: identity (k=0, flip=False) in all eval examples [observed]
  output: dst outline with each hole flood-filled by matched src subsprite color, tight-cropped

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Design a "cavity template" — an LR-symmetric layout of 4-9 cavity slots, each with
      (row_rank, col_rank, center_position, seed_bbox). Layout defines POSITIONS only;
      shapes come from the next steps. Pack slots tightly (allow diagonal-adjacent slots).
    - Build the output grid (filled dst) by mutating each template slot's shape independently
      — start from the seed bbox and randomly add/remove boundary cells while keeping the
      cavity 4-connected. Aim for ~50% non-rectangular mutations (L, T, cross, staircase,
      notched rectangles, organic blobs). Neighboring cavities are ALLOWED to touch
      diagonally (4-disconnected, 8-connected). Assign a fill color to each cavity. Wrap
      the entire fill mask in a 1-cell outline (outline cells are the bg neighbors of any
      fill cell under 4-connectivity). LR-symmetry is maintained by mutating mirror-pair
      slots with mirrored operations.
    - Derive dst from output by replacing all fill pixels with bg. The result is a single
      8-connected outline-only object with empty holes in the same positions as src's
      cavities.
    - Independently build src from the same cavity template by mutating each slot's shape
      AGAIN with a FRESH random seed — src subsprite shapes MUST visibly differ from dst
      hole shapes. Wrap with outline and fill
      each cavity with the assigned color. src is 1 connected component. Do NOT reuse the
      dst shape array for src — always run the mutation independently.
    - Place src and dst on a 22-30 x 22-30 bg canvas. They may overlap spatially as long
      as pixels don't collide. Verify main(input) == expected output.
```
</generation_spec>
